# PART I — VISUAL DESIGN SYSTEM

## 1. TWO THEMES, ONE BRAND

The website must support two complete visual themes: Dark and Light.

The theme toggle must switch the entire design system, including backgrounds, typography, illustrations, borders, shadows, image treatments, controls, modals, menus, and animations.

The two themes must feel intentionally art-directed, not like a basic CSS color inversion.

### DARK THEME — MAGNETIC NIGHT

Core palette:

- Primary background: #080808
- Secondary background: #111111
- Elevated surface: #191919
- Primary accent: #ED2028
- Accent hover: #FF343C
- Primary text: #F0ECE8
- Secondary text: #AAA5A2
- Borders: rgba(240, 236, 232, 0.14)
- Subtle red glow: rgba(237, 32, 40, 0.20)

Pure white must NOT be a primary background color in Dark mode.

Use warm off-white for text and restrained neutral highlights. Keep the visual world predominantly black, charcoal, and red.

Design characteristics:
- Deep, immersive black surfaces.
- Dramatic red focal points.
- Restrained red illumination around selected interactive elements.
- Fine technical grid lines.
- Animated magnetic-field graphics.
- Subtle grain or texture only where performance permits.
- High-contrast typography.
- Layered images and overlapping compositions.
- Thin borders and intentional negative space.
- Selected elements that appear to emerge from darkness.

Red should be visually powerful because it is used selectively. Do not flood every section with red.

### LIGHT THEME — MAGNETIC PAPER

Core palette:

- Primary background: #FFFFFF
- Secondary background: #FFF5F5
- Elevated surface: #FFFFFF
- Soft red surface: #FCE5E5
- Primary accent: #D71920
- Accent hover: #B9141B
- Primary text: #171313
- Secondary text: #62595A
- Borders: rgba(80, 20, 20, 0.13)
- Subtle red shadow: rgba(180, 20, 30, 0.10)

Pure white is allowed in Light mode.

Design characteristics:
- Clean editorial layouts.
- White space balanced with soft red surfaces.
- Deep, readable typography.
- Red typography accents and graphic lines.
- Light, precise borders.
- Subtle paper-like layering where appropriate.
- Soft shadows rather than dark, heavy shadows.
- Clear separation between primary content and supporting information.

Light mode must not become a plain white page with red buttons. It should have the same level of depth, visual rhythm, and art direction as Dark mode.

### THEME IMPLEMENTATION

Create centralized theme tokens using the existing project's design system or CSS custom properties.

For example:

--color-background
--color-surface
--color-surface-elevated
--color-text-primary
--color-text-secondary
--color-accent
--color-accent-hover
--color-border
--color-shadow
--color-glow

Do not scatter hardcoded colors throughout individual components.

Use semantic tokens for every major UI element.

Requirements:
- Add an accessible theme toggle in the main navigation.
- Provide clear Sun/Moon or equivalent icons.
- Animate theme changes subtly, without flashing or excessive transitions.
- Preserve the user's selected theme across visits.
- On the first visit, use the system preference unless a deliberate brand-default setting is configured.
- Avoid a flash of the wrong theme during initial rendering.
- Support keyboard operation and screen readers.
- Ensure both themes work on every route, modal, dropdown, and responsive layout.
- Check contrast and readability in both modes.
- Do not change layout, content, or navigation when switching themes.
- Provide theme-aware logo and illustration variants where necessary.

